.docname {Packages}
.include {docs}

A **package**, called an *atom*, is a published, reusable bundle of Quarkdown sources and assets.

The official `@atoms` repository can be found at [`quarkdown-labs/atoms`](https://github.com/quarkdown-labs/atoms).

## Using a package

Reference a package from `.include` with the `@scope/name:version` syntax:

```markdown
.include {@atoms/simple-cv:1.0.0}
```

- `@scope` refers to the repository or namespace identifier. `@atoms` is currently the only supported one.
- `simple-cv` is the package name.
- `1.0.0` is the package version. Note that versions in the `@atoms` scope are immutable.

The first time a document references a package, Quarkdown downloads it into your project:

.filetree
    - my-project/
      - @atoms/
        - simple-cv/
          - atom.toml
          - main.qd
          - ...
    - main.qd

Installing packages is covered by the `package-install` [permission](cli-compiler.qd#permissions), which is granted by default.

### Version control

Whether to gitignore the `@atoms` directory or not is not enforced. Keep it tracked for offline builds, or ignore it for full reproducibility.

## Publishing a package to `@atoms`

Please follow the instructions on [`quarkdown-labs/atoms`](https://github.com/quarkdown-labs/atoms) to publish your own package to the official repository.
